  "notes": "Basis: governmental funds modified (cash) basis, enterprise funds accrual; basis recorded as cash. Governmental lines use the Total Governmental Funds column (printed on p6, labels on p5). 'Taxes' 34,223 split using General fund Schedule 2 (p10: property tax 469, motor vehicle 4,001; the 4,470 General 'Taxes' column on p5), Street Schedule 6 (p14: property tax 18,822, county road tax 1,444) and nonmajor Schedule 4 (p12: property tax 9,487). Business-type lines are from Exhibit H (p8); business_type measure is net position (accrual statement); transfers from other funds 98,624 recorded as transfers_net. Business-type reported receipts total computed (no single printed total excluding transfers). proprietary left null (statement is not GAAP; cash flow statement on p9 not extracted). Balance sheet uses Exhibit A Totals 2025 column (mix of modified cash governmental and accrual business-type); consumer deposits listed as other liabilities. Schedule 7 (p15 combined budget, budgetary-basis actuals that include proprietary funds) and Schedule 9 (p16 Keno fund, actual column duplicates Schedule 6 plus budgetary adjustment) not recorded in detail to avoid double counting; Schedules 3 (p11) and 5 (p13) are balance sheets only. Gov roll-forward: 347,552 + 376,340 - 401,967 + 10,141 - 108,765 = 223,301. Added business-type lines (Sewer, Water receipts and disbursements, budgetary-basis actuals) from Schedule 7 (p15) to detail, since no other schedule details those funds; budget printed '-' for each (budget is held in the General All Purpose total), so budget_final null; no business-type total printed. Read pages 1-16 of 16. Schedule 7 Sewer receipts 121,105 split into revenue 22,481 and an other financing (transfer in) line 98,624, per the Exhibit I cash flows (p9)."
